-- Conaturals, split out of stream.nova: the ν-scheme at its
-- simplest sum polynomial (NovaFoundation.txt, "Coinductive
-- types"). conat ≔ ν (K 𝟙 ⊎ 𝕏): zero observes as inj₁, a successor
-- as inj₂ of its predecessor; ∞ is its own predecessor. The three
-- constructors are COPATTERN items (NovaElaboration.txt, "Defining
-- observations"): each states its one observation and the macro
-- synthesizes the corecursor (czero and csucc stop, cinf continues),
-- the β-shaped observation lemma (czeroOut, cinfOut, csuccOut) and
-- the uniqueness lemma (czeroEta, cinfEta, csuccEta) — coinduction
-- at the graph invariant. infSucc is the classic coinductive
-- theorem, by el-nu-coind directly.

def conat : 𝕌 ≔ ν (K 𝟙 ⊎ 𝕏)

def czero : conat using (conat.unfold)
  | out czero ≔ inj₁ ()

def cinf : conat using (conat.unfold)
  | out cinf ≔ inj₂ cinf

-- csucc: emit inj₂ and STOP at the stored predecessor — csuccOut
-- releases it bare at ANY predecessor, by β (primitive corecursion)
def csucc : conat → conat using (conat.unfold)
  | out (csucc n) ≔ inj₂ n

-- conat's classic coinductive theorem: ∞ is its own successor. The
-- closure exercises the relator's SUM clause: the ⊎-elim at motive Ω
-- is stuck at the generic observations, un-stuck by the invariant's
-- variable-definition equations, and collapses definitionally on the
-- inj₂/inj₂ diagonal — where the up-to-equality hole closes by
-- reflexivity (inj₂ ⋆).
def infSucc : cinf ≡ csucc cinf using (cinf.eq, csucc.eq, hyp.rw, conat.unfold) ≔
  coind (x y. ∥(x ≡ cinf ∈ conat) × (y ≡ csucc cinf ∈ conat)∥)
    (⋆ (⋆, ⋆))
    (x y h. squash-elim h (w. ⋆ (inj₂ ⋆)))
